on's cash edge can close the gap in a district where the incumbent already lost renomination.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Cory Mills (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Cory Mills lost renomination, leaving this R+5 Central Florida seat open. Republican Ryan Elijah, backed by local sheriffs, faces Democrat Bale Dalton, who has outraised him roughly three to one and benefits from DCCC attack ads against Elijah. The race is genuinely contested: a DCCC poll showed a dead heat, and two forecasters call it a Tossup.\n\nStill, the district's Republican lean, a late pullback of House Majority PAC spending on Dalton's behalf, and prediction markets pricing the GOP near 98% suggest the edge rests with Elijah. A narrow Republican win is most likely, but the margin is small enough that a strong Democratic turnout effort could flip the seat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4211, "margin": -1.21}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4651, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3497, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3248, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2949, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3493, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3328, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3464, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3386, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3794, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3754, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3743, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4206, "margin": -1.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3495, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3089, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2915, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3164, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.3185, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.3207, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0